FORMAT 1
SCENARIO Rejected push
LABEL    Worksheet 4 · dry run
SUMMARY  Someone pushed to GitHub in the meantime. What git push does and how to fix it.
INTRO    You are **Petr**. You and your classmate Anna share the repository **shared-cookbook** and you have cloned it. Anna has just pushed her recipe – you do not know about it yet.
INTRO    On the right you see the history on your computer and GitHub below it.

SETUP
  PERSON anna NAME "Anna Svobodová" EMAIL "svobodovaa@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "anna-svobodova" LABEL "Anna's computer"
  PERSON petr NAME "Petr Dvořák" EMAIL "dvorakp@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "petr-dvorak" LABEL "Petr's computer"
  MACHINE anna CONFIGURED HIDDEN
  MACHINE petr CONFIGURED
  REPOSITORY git/shared-cookbook
  GITHUB anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook README COLLABORATOR petr-dvorak
  AS petr
  PS> mkdir git
  PS> cd git
  PS> git clone https://github.com/anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook.git
  PS> cd shared-cookbook
  AS anna
  PS> mkdir git
  PS> cd git
  PS> git clone https://github.com/anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook.git
  PS> cd shared-cookbook
  FILE potato-soup.md
    # Potato soup

    - 4 potatoes
    - 1 onion
    - marjoram
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add potato soup"
  PS> git push
  AS petr
  VSCODE git/shared-cookbook
END

TASK Create a file **buns.md** with a recipe and commit it.
  HINT  git add buns.md
  HINT  git commit -m "Add buns"
  CHECK file buns.md in HEAD exists
END

TASK Try to push.
  HINT     git push
  QUESTION What happened? Read the hint lines.
  CHECK    output of "git push..." contains "[rejected]"
END

TASK Download Anna's commit. **MERGE_MSG** opens – do not change anything, just close it.
  HINT     git pull
  QUESTION Which new commit appeared in the graph and how many parents does it have?
  CHECK    HEAD is a merge
END

TASK Push again.
  HINT  git push
  CHECK github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook main equals HEAD
  CHECK HEAD is a merge
END
